      "message": "Agree so.\n\nI think we can do generic splitting that for 4 combinations of flags (XFER_START, XFER_STOP), however, what I\u0027m not sure is if we should do outer retry when one of them is failed.\n\nFor example. Originally, the caller invokes\ni2c_xfer() 6 times manually with flag XFER_START, 0, 0, 0, 0, XFER_STOP\n\nShould we really do retry if saying that fourth chip_i2c_xfer() failed ?\n\nFurthermore, if originally, the caller invokes\ni2c_xfer() 6 times manually with flag 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, XFER_STOP \nI\u0027m not quite sure what retry logic should be done here even if we see a EC_ERROR_BUSY.",
